        code: '7121',
        major_group: '7',
        sub_major_group: '71',
        minor_group: '712',
        unit_group: '7121',
        title: 'Roofers',
        definition: 'Roofers build and repair roofs on all types of buildings using one or more kinds of material.',
        tasks_include: "Tasks include -\n(a)  studying drawings, specifications and construction sites to determine materials required;\n(b)  covering roof frameworks with slate and pre-fabricated tiles to cover pitched roofs;\n(c)  laying a waterproof shield and fixing metallic or synthetic materials to a building’s frame;\n(d)  sizing and cutting roofing materials to fit around edges, corners and protuberances such as chimneys;\n(e)  using natural materials such as thatching to provide roof coverings;\n(f)  creating temporary structures such as scaffolding and ladders.",
        excluded_occupations: null,
        notes: 'Installers of metal roofing are classified in Unit Group 7121: Roofers. Workers who make sheet metal products for adaptation and installation by roofers are classified in Unit Group 7213: Sheet Metal Workers.',
