        code: '8311',
        major_group: '8',
        sub_major_group: '83',
        minor_group: '831',
        unit_group: '8311',
        title: 'Locomotive Engine Drivers',
        definition: 'Locomotive engine drivers drive, or assist in driving, locomotive engines to transport passengers and freight.',
        tasks_include: "Tasks include -\n(a)  driving or assisting in driving a steam, electric or diesel-electric locomotive engine;\n(b)  driving an underground or elevated passenger train;\n(c)  driving a locomotive to haul carriages underground or on the surface of a mine or quarry;\n(d)  watching for track hazards, observing signals and indicator gauges;\n(e)  operating communications systems to communicate with train crews and traffic controllers to ensure safe operation and scheduling of trains.",
        excluded_occupations: "Some related occupations classified elsewhere:\n- Tram driver - 8331",
        notes: 'Drivers of vehicles that operate on fixed rail systems that are separated from public roadways are classified in Unit Group 8311: Locomotive Engine Drivers. Drivers of vehicles for passenger transportation on fixed rails that are incorporated in the public roadway are classified in Unit Group 8331: Bus and Tram Drivers.',
